dialogue cohesion_generic_tank_healer
title: The count of wounds
trigger: Cohesion role:Tank role:Healer level=4
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker with $with
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  The Healer sits beside the Tank with a lamp and a needle, closing the last cut of the day. Neither says much. They've done this many times now.
  -> count

node count hero
  Eleven today. I count them, every one. Eleven blows that would have landed on someone else if you hadn't stepped in front.
  -> sure

node sure with
  That's the work. You stand at the back and keep us breathing. I stand at the front and keep them busy. It's a fair trade.
  -> fair

node fair hero
  It isn't fair. You take the wound and I take the thanks. Commander, tell the Tank to stop stepping in front of everything.
  * The Tank stands there because the Healer is behind. That's the whole trust between you. -> trust
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 10
  * Fewer steps forward, then. I'd rather the Tank whole for the next fight. -> fewer
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 6
  * Counting wounds won't help anyone. Let it go. -> letgo
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -4

node trust with
  Behind me. Aye. I don't look back to check. I never have to.
  -> mark

node fewer with
  Fewer. I can try fewer. Not none.
  -> mark

node letgo hero
  I can't let it go. It's the only way I know what you cost.
  -> mark

node mark with
  Here. You've been saying the count out loud for weeks. Mark it somewhere, if you need it marked. On the shield, where I'll see it.
  -> shield

node shield hero
  On the shield. A notch for every one I closed.
  * Do it. Let the shield carry what the two of you carry. -> notch
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 8
  * Mark the ones you both came home from, not the wounds. -> home
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 9
  * A shield is no ledger. Keep it clean. -> clean
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -2

node notch with
  Eleven, then. Start tonight. I'll wear the count into every fight.
  -> close

node home hero
  The ones we came home from. That's a better count. That one I'd like to see grow.
  -> close

node clean with
  Clean it stays. The count can live with you, then. I trust you to keep it.
  -> close

node close commander
  The lamp burns low. The Healer ties off the last stitch, and the Tank flexes the arm and calls it good as new, which it isn't, quite.
